  "notes": "{徐々|じょじょ}に emphasizes a slow, steady pace of change without abrupt shifts. The kanji {徐|じょ} means \"slowly\" and is repeated for emphasis.\n\nPOSITION IN SENTENCE:\nTypically placed directly before the verb it modifies: {徐々|じょじょ}に⟦{変|か}わる→変わる：00714_kawaru⟧, {徐々|じょじょ}に⟦{増|ふ}える→増える：01183_fueru⟧.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {徐々|じょじょ}に⟦{回復|かいふく}する→回復する：21330_kaifukusuru⟧: to gradually recover\n- {徐々|じょじょ}に⟦{慣|な}れる→慣れる：00870_nareru⟧: to gradually get used to\n- {徐々|じょじょ}に⟦{増|ふ}える→増える：01183_fueru⟧: to gradually increase\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {徐々|じょじょ}に: slowly, steadily (slightly formal)\n- ⟦だんだん→だんだん：00832_dandan⟧: gradually (casual, everyday)\n- ⟦{次第|しだい}に→次第に：05531_shidaini⟧: increasingly, progressively (literary/formal)\n- ⟦ゆっくり→ゆっくり：00910_yukkuri⟧: slowly (focuses on speed, not progression)",
